# Two turbines onto one generator that cannot eat them.
#
# A turbine makes 120 rotary and a generator takes 70 a tick and not one more,
# so half of what the second turbine makes turns against a full port and goes
# nowhere. The fix is a second generator, and the reason to build this first is
# that the drive makes the mistake *visible*: two straight bright lines
# converging on a machine plainly too small for both of them.
#
# The version of this design before the transport family went had a line shaft
# in the middle, and it is worth saying what the shaft was actually doing here,
# because the answer is nothing. Two turbines could always feed one port; the
# port shares what arrives; six machines could always hang off one drive. None
# of that was the shaft. The shaft was a four-tile component that let the two
# turbines sit four tiles further from the generator than they needed to, and
# charged one percent for it.

machine "One Generator"
brief power

reactor   R1  at 0,0   throttle 50

exchanger HX1 at 5,0
exchanger HX2 at 5,4

turbine   T1  at 9,0
turbine   T2  at 9,4

generator G1  at 14,2

pump      W1  at 0,5

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W1.water -> HX2.water

wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T2.steam

wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G1.rotary
